  "name": "scatter_pie_2020",
  "description": "The Modern eclectic synthesis (Mallory & Adams, *The Oxford Introduction to Proto-Indo-European*, 2006; Fortson, *Indo-European Language and Culture*, 2010; Beekes, *Comparative Indo-European Linguistics*, 2011).  Mostly continues the post-Hittite Standard but admits Glottalic as a live alternative.  No single consensus on the phonetic values of the stop series; the laryngeals' phonetic identity also debated (h₁ as /ʔ/ vs /h/; h₂ as /ħ/ or /χ/; h₃ as /ʕʷ/ or /ɣʷ/).  Three stop series × five places + three laryngeals.  RECONSTRUCTED, NOT ATTESTED.  150+ years of revision later, the orthodoxy has NOT converged on a single phonetic interpretation.  25 cells filled.",
